1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:06,840
Singapore's Building and Construction Authority has consulted on changes to the strata management law.

2
00:00:07,190 --> 00:00:12,570
MCSTs that scan and index their core records now will find the proposals easier to meet.

3
00:00:13,070 --> 00:00:28,070
In its consultation from 9 March to 8 April 2026, BCA proposed that owners could get copies of records without first viewing them, and that unpaid fees should no longer excuse a service provider holding back MCST documents.

4
00:00:28,570 --> 00:00:34,930
BCA also proposed that notices could be served electronically, and that by-laws could be lodged online.

5
00:00:35,280 --> 00:00:39,420
Every notice and resolution then needs a clean digital source file.

6
00:00:39,920 --> 00:00:49,400
Start with the strata roll and by-laws, then meeting minutes, budgets and audited accounts, essential facilities records, and building plans.

7
00:00:49,750 --> 00:00:53,040
Index each file by record type, date and meeting.

8
00:00:53,540 --> 00:00:59,930
These records hold owners' personal data, so limit access by role and redact copies, not originals.

9
00:01:00,280 --> 00:01:05,320
These were proposals, so check BCA's website for when any change takes effect.

10
00:01:05,820 --> 00:01:12,410
Micrographics Data scans and indexes strata records, collected by our own staff in our own vehicles.

11
00:01:12,760 --> 00:01:15,720
Request a quote at micrographicsdata.com.
